.TH TATAMI\-MKPKG 8 "" "tatami"
.SH NAME
tatami\-mkpkg \- build tatami packages from a recipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tatami\-mkpkg
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tatami\-mkpkg
reads a recipe, the
.BR Tatamifile ,
in the current directory, builds the software it describes into a staging directory
and packs the result into a package for
.BR tatami (8).
The recipe format is that of the pkgutils
.BR Pkgfile ,
with real dependency fields.
.PP
The package is named
.IB name _ version [\- release ]_ arch . extension
for example
.BR zlib_1.3.2\-1_x86_64.tar.pkg ,
and is written to the output directory.
.SH THE TATAMIFILE
The recipe is a bash fragment.
A line of the form
.B # Description: \fItext\fR
gives the package a description.
.TP
.B name, version
Required. Names and versions may not contain an underscore; the name must start with
a letter or digit.
.TP
.B release
Optional; the package version becomes
.IB version \- release\fR.
.TP
.B source
An array of files or URLs.
URLs are downloaded next to the recipe unless the file is already there;
other files are taken from the recipe's directory.
If a file
.B .md5sum
exists, the sources are checked against it.
Archives (tar, zip) are unpacked into the source directory, other files copied.
.TP
.B depends, conflicts, provides, replaces
Arrays of relations, one per element:
.BR libfoo ,
.BR "libbar >= 2.0" ,
.BR "a | b" .
An element may not contain a comma.
.TP
.B arch
Required. There is no default:
without it (or with an empty value) tatami\-mkpkg prints
.B Error: arch is not defined in Tatamifile
and exits with status 1.
Use the target architecture, or
.B noarch
for architecture\-independent packages.
It is never taken from the configuration or the build machine.
.BR noarch ,
.B all
and
.B any
mean a package that is not tied to an architecture.
.TP
.B build()
Required. It is run in the source directory
.RB ( $SRC )
and must install into
.BR $PKG ,
for example with
.BR "make DESTDIR=$PKG install" .
.SS Example
.nf
# Description: Compression library
name=zlib
version=1.3.2
release=1
source=(https://example.org/zlib\-$version.tar.gz)

build() {
        cd zlib\-$version
        ./configure \-\-prefix=/usr
        make
        make DESTDIR=$PKG install
}
.fi
.SH INSTALL SCRIPTS
If a file named
.B tatami.install
exists in the same directory as the
.BR Tatamifile ,
it is bundled automatically into the root of the package as the hidden file
.BR .INSTALL ;
nothing needs to be set in the recipe.
It may define two bash functions:
.TP
.B pre_install
Run by
.BR tatami (8)
before the package's files are extracted. If it exits non\-zero the whole
transaction is rolled back.
.TP
.B post_install
Run after the transaction was committed. A failure is only reported.
.PP
Both receive the package version as their argument and find the installation root in
.BR TATAMI_ROOT .
There are no scripts for removal.
.B .INSTALL
is not installed as a file.
.SH SIGNING
If a signing key exists, the build signs its results as part of the build.
The key is the file named by the environment variable
.B TATAMI_PRIVKEY
(which must exist), otherwise
.BR ~/.tatami/privkey ;
it is made with
.BR "tatami keygen" .
Right after the package is written,
.B tatami\-mkpkg
.IP \(bu 3
refreshes the index
.B repo.solv
of the output directory, which records the SHA\-256 checksum of every package in it,
.IP \(bu 3
signs the package, writing
.IB package .sig,
.IP \(bu 3
signs the index, writing
.BR repo.solv.sig .
.PP
Publish all of these files together; clients put the public key (the
.B .pub
file made by
.BR "tatami keygen" )
into
.B /etc/tatami/keys/
(see
.BR tatami.conf (5)).
Without a key, packages are built unsigned and the output directory is not indexed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIrecipe\fP
Recipe to build (default
.BR Tatamifile ).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIdir\fP
Where to put the package (default: the current directory).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fP
Use this configuration file instead of
.BR /etc/tatami/tatami.conf .
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-compression " " \fIc\fP
One of
.BR gz ,
.BR zst ,
.BR xz ,
.BR bz2 ,
.BR lz4 ,
.B lzma
or
.BR none .
The default is the one chosen when tatami was built
.RB ( PKG_COMPRESSION ,
.B zst
unless changed), unless the package extension itself names one.
It cannot be set in the configuration or the environment.
Compression is done by tatami itself.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-work
Do not remove the work directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-bulkhead ", " \-\-no\-sandbox
Build on the host, without the sandbox.
.TP
.B \-\-bulkhead
Use the sandbox even if the configuration turns it off.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sign
Do not sign, even if a key exists.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.SH SANDBOX
By default
.B build()
runs in a
.BR bwrap (1)
sandbox, started through
.BR "tatami bulkhead" :
the system is read\-only, the network is unshared, and only a temporary
build directory and the package root are writable.
The sandbox is required then; if
.B bwrap
is missing the build fails instead of running unprotected.
It can be turned off with
.BR \-\-no\-bulkhead
or
.BR "BULKHEAD = no"
in
.BR tatami.conf (5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TATAMI
The tatami binary used for packing, indexing, signing and the sandbox
(default: found in
.BR PATH ).
.TP
.B TATAMI_PRIVKEY
The signing key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B Tatamifile
The recipe.
.TP
.B tatami.install
Optional install script, bundled as
.BR .INSTALL .
.TP
.B .md5sum
Optional checksums of the sources.
.TP
.B /etc/tatami/tatami.conf
Configuration (only the key
.B BULKHEAD
is used; the package extension and compression are fixed when tatami is built).
.TP
.B ~/.tatami/privkey
The default signing key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
if the package was built, non\-zero otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tatami (8),
.BR tatami.conf (5)
